<%# A tab's accessible name is its label alone, so the icon contributes none:
    hidden from the accessibility tree and out of the tab order. The spec rules
    it because an icon that names itself gives the tab a compound name and
    breaks exact selection in the browser lane - so the rule lives here once
    rather than in every tab, where the next one could quietly get it wrong. %>
<svg class="tab-bar__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <%= yield %>
</svg>
